## Why This Is Asked

Gauges a candidate's ability to design streaming, scalable PCA with missing data and drift in production environments.

## Key Concepts

- Incremental PCA / SVD, sliding window approaches
- Online imputation for missing data, streaming normalization
- Drift detection in loadings and explained variance
- Real-time alerting tied to interpretable loadings

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: incremental update sketch
let components = initPCA(12);
for (each batch) {
  let X = imputeOnline(batch);
  X = normalize(X);
  components = updateSVD(components, X);
  let loadings = computeLoadings(components);
  if (driftDetected(loadings)) alert(loadings);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate latency budgets under burst traffic?
- Which metrics would you monitor to avoid false alerts in drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical PCA deployment in a streaming, real-world telemetry context with missing data and the need for interpretable components. It probes method selection, online updating, drift handling, and actionable alerting under latency constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming PCA variants (IPCA, PPCA, Sparse PCA)
- Handling missing data online
- Component interpretability via sparsity and rotation
- Drift detection on loadings and actionable alerts
- Latency budgeting in edge-to-cloud pipelines

## Code Example
````javascript
// Pseudo: online update loop snippet
for (event of stream) {
  x = impute(event.features);
  x = scale(x);
  subspace = ipca.partial_fit(x);
  score = reconstruct_error(x, subspace);
  if (drift_detected(subspace.loadings)) alert();
}
````

